Error [jet.ValueThrownAway]: This Payment.Client value is thrown away
  --> tests/ui/protocol_out_of_order.jet:18:8
    |
 18 |     h1.Charge(500) ?? panic("charge failed")
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `run` has no return type, so it returns nothing and the value of its last line is lost
 Fix: If `run` should return it, write `-> Payment.Client` after its parameter list; to discard it on purpose, write `.drop("reason")`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0433

Error [jet.TypestateWrongState]: `Charge` needs `Payment.Client.S2`, but `h1` is `Payment.Client.S1`
  --> tests/ui/protocol_out_of_order.jet:18:8
    |
 18 |     h1.Charge(500) ?? panic("charge failed")
    |        ^^^^^^
 Why: Typestate: `Charge` takes only `Payment.Client.S2`; calling it with `Payment.Client` in another state is the out-of-order bug the state list rules out
 Fix: Moves from `Payment.Client.S1`: `recv_Ack`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
